00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:40.000
Let it loose, man.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:41.710
So one of the things that Shepherd and I

00:03:41.710 --> 00:03:43.820
do together is ride bikes.

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:47.750
We don't do it so often,

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:49.790
for me to say that it's our thing.

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:50.790
I know that you and Lincoln

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:53.618
have gotten into mountain biking together.

00:03:53.618 --> 00:03:56.470
Yeah, he's not huge into it.

00:03:56.470 --> 00:03:59.440
Every time I asked him to do
it he reluctantly says yes,

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:01.910
well not every, most of the time.

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:04.910
And Lando has a bike and
I'll take them biking.

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:08.440
I mean we all dreamed
about the idea of, as a dad

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:10.097
just being able to say,

00:04:10.097 --> 00:04:12.920
"Hey, let's go do," fill in the blank.

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:16.890
And lights in our kids
eyes just turning on

00:04:16.890 --> 00:04:18.850
and then being so excited

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:21.530
to go spend the day of adventure with dad.

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:24.030
Well that only happens in the movies.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:25.930
And it probably happens in their memories

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:27.610
they're probably gonna remember it finally

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:29.820
but in the moment it's
like, "Do I have to go?"

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:31.250
When I mentioned riding a bike

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:32.670
the light goes off in their eyes.

00:04:32.670 --> 00:04:33.503
Right.

00:04:33.503 --> 00:04:34.800
What happened to us Link?

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.690
I don't know.
Video games.

00:04:36.690 --> 00:04:38.453
But I have noticed that Lincoln,

00:04:39.410 --> 00:04:44.410
as we're starting to allow
him to see some friends

00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:49.570
in very controlled open air environments,

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:54.193
