Well you kinda learn
that right at the top.

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:43.913
Okay, good.

00:05:44.970 --> 00:05:47.500
Also you can't spoil a movie
that's several decades old.

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:48.333
That an impossibility.

00:05:48.333 --> 00:05:50.460
I know, I was just playing into the Link

00:05:50.460 --> 00:05:51.570
You should watch it though.

00:05:51.570 --> 00:05:54.040
And that, yes, that's one.

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:57.140
If you didn't think Ferris
Bueller would wow you,

00:05:57.140 --> 00:05:59.240
Stand By Me is a different level of movie.

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:04.240
It is a intense, joyous, but sad.

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:07.873
I mean, it's just a beautiful,
beautiful movie, anyway.

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:10.186
You and Shepherd are biking.

00:06:10.186 --> 00:06:11.510
So I decide to go biking with Shepherd

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:14.810
and this is the first time that we have,

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:16.420
you just watered your dog with your mug.

00:06:16.420 --> 00:06:18.373
I didn't realize I was so full.

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:22.450
So we decided to go out,
and you know how it is.

00:06:22.450 --> 00:06:27.450
I mean, for some reason,
when you make a decision

00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:30.740
to be like, I'm going to go out

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:32.520
and I'm going to ride bikes with my son.

00:06:32.520 --> 00:06:33.353
I'm going to take his
bike down from the place

00:06:33.353 --> 00:06:35.590
You want it to be relatively easy.

00:06:35.590 --> 00:06:37.380
You want to be like, okay
I'm gonna take his bike down

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:39.100
from the place that is
hanging in the garage,

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:40.730
and we're going to put it on the bike rack

00:06:40.730 --> 00:06:41.817
and we're going to drive to the place

00:06:41.817 --> 00:06:42.767
that we're going to bike.

00:06:42.767 --> 00:06:45.240
But no, but of course, of course,

00:06:45.240 --> 00:06:46.467
when I pull his bike down,

00:06:46.467 --> 00:06:49.780
out of nowhere, his tires flat.

00:06:49.780 --> 00:06:50.750
I knew you were gonna say that.

00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:53.990
Do you remember ever having a
flat tire when we were kids?

00:06:53.990 --> 00:06:56.340
No, but it's something--
California.

00:06:56.340 --> 00:06:58.320
There's some California spurs.

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:01.330
Because I feel like I rode

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:04.340
the same bike tires and inner tubes.

00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:07.330
Never once changed--
Like my entire childhood,

00:07:07.330 --> 00:07:08.530
or at least when I got a bike

00:07:08.530 --> 00:07:10.750
I kept that bike and those inner tubes.

00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:13.050
Never had it, I had to pump
up the tires occasionally.

00:07:13.050 --> 00:07:15.240
Let me tell you jack.
Tell me jack.

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:19.017
There were some sand spurs
back in North Carolina too.

00:07:19.017 --> 00:07:20.942
But we never hit 'em.

00:07:20.942 --> 00:07:22.210
I don't know what it is.

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:27.210
But yes, okay, so had
to patch the inner tube,

00:07:28.220 --> 00:07:30.310
because I didn't have a replacement.

00:07:30.310 --> 00:07:32.560
Of course this requires
taking the wheel off.

00:07:33.848 --> 00:07:35.700
And then I got to put it back on.

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:38.450
It was the front tire,
thankfully, a little bit easier.

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:41.890
And then we're like, okay.

00:07:41.890 --> 00:07:44.640
And I kind of got mad at that point.

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:48.110
Did you invite Shepherd to
help you patch the tire?

00:07:48.110 --> 00:07:50.170
Because that's a dad choice.

00:07:50.170 --> 00:07:51.250
I thought about it.

00:07:51.250 --> 00:07:52.730
All right son, you know what we're gonna

00:07:52.730 --> 00:07:54.235
learn to patch a tire together,

00:07:54.235 --> 00:07:55.490
because I don't know how to do it either,.

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:57.680
No, I do know how to do it
because I've had to do it

00:07:57.680 --> 00:07:59.340
like five times since
living in California.

00:07:59.340 --> 00:08:02.513
But he was, like I got the bike down.

00:08:02.513 --> 00:08:03.930
I was like, "Oh man, you got a flat tire."

00:08:03.930 --> 00:08:05.627
And he was like, "Okay,
I'm going upstairs.

00:08:05.627 --> 00:08:07.430
"Let me know when you're ready."

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:08.830
And then I was just like,

00:08:08.830 --> 00:08:11.310
okay, I'm not, I don't
want to fight him here.

00:08:11.310 --> 00:08:12.830
Because I'm having to
fight him to go ride bikes.

00:08:12.830 --> 00:08:14.810
If you force him to change it,

00:08:14.810 --> 00:08:15.790
he's not gonna ride it with you.

00:08:15.790 --> 00:08:17.290
So let me, 'cause this is a key point,

00:08:17.290 --> 00:08:20.590
I'm already a little bit in a bad mood.

00:08:20.590 --> 00:08:22.640
Fix the bike, put the bike on the rack.

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:25.090
We go to the place that
we're going to ride.

00:08:25.090 --> 00:08:27.810
And Shepherd's already complaining.

00:08:27.810 --> 00:08:30.327
He's like, "Dad, my bike hurts me

00:08:30.327 --> 00:08:34.260
"and my legs get cramped, is too small."

00:08:34.260 --> 00:08:36.617
And I'm like, "Okay, well, first of all,

00:08:36.617 --> 00:08:38.507
"it's not that small."

00:08:38.507 --> 00:08:41.297
"And if you can go out

00:08:41.297 --> 00:08:44.312
"and do the things that
I'm asking you to do today,

00:08:44.312 --> 00:08:46.767
[Link And Rhett Together]
I'll get you a new bike.

00:08:46.767 --> 00:08:50.500
I've been through all of this too.

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:54.300
I mean, all of the flat
tires, all of the bribery.

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:55.650
Promising new bikes.
Yeah.

00:08:55.650 --> 00:08:56.747
And so I said,

00:08:56.747 --> 00:08:59.027
"Shepherd, the thing that
we're going to concentrate on

00:08:59.027 --> 00:09:03.430
"today is you being able
to stand up and pedal."

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:06.230
because he'll do it, but he
doesn't quite get his weight,

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:07.950
he's really using his quads,

00:09:07.950 --> 00:09:09.640
and I'm trying to get him to understand,

00:09:09.640 --> 00:09:13.910
standing up while riding your
bike is how you get power.

00:09:13.910 --> 00:09:16.330
It's how you go up hills.

00:09:16.330 --> 00:09:20.160
This is a quintessential skill set

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:22.960
that I'm trying to pass on to my kids.

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:25.440
And by the time I was
11 years old, of course,

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:26.390
I could stand up on a bike

00:09:26.390 --> 00:09:28.310
because all we did was ride bikes around.

00:09:28.310 --> 00:09:30.500
But the only time that we
ride bikes as a family,

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:32.610
is when we ride bikes as a family,

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:33.443
You know what I'm saying.

00:09:33.443 --> 00:09:36.010
It's like he's not riding his
bike around the neighborhood.

00:09:36.010 --> 00:09:37.270
I don't know exactly know why

00:09:37.270 --> 00:09:38.730
it's probably because
we've got so many hills

00:09:38.730 --> 00:09:39.880
and it would be really difficult.

00:09:39.880 --> 00:09:42.294
But anyway, we get out there--

00:09:42.294 --> 00:09:43.557
Specially if you can't stand up.

00:09:43.557 --> 00:09:46.053
And we're in a relatively flat area.

00:09:46.930 --> 00:09:51.930
But instead of taking the
concrete path or the paved paths

00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:56.080
that we would normally
take around this big area.

00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:57.000
I was like, let's go down

00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:59.113
into some of these
little trails and stuff.

00:09:59.113 --> 00:10:01.590
It's not like a mountain
biking area necessarily.

00:10:01.590 --> 00:10:05.000
It's more of a walking area,
but mountain bikes are allowed.

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:06.850
And I just noticed really early on

00:10:06.850 --> 00:10:08.633
that Shepherd is lagging behind.

00:10:09.753 --> 00:10:12.350
And so I'll get ahead
of him then I'll go back

00:10:12.350 --> 00:10:13.183
and be like, "All right, Shepherd,

00:10:13.183 --> 00:10:14.930
"you got to keep up with
me, I mean this is flat."

00:10:14.930 --> 00:10:16.577
I mean, there's nothing.

00:10:16.577 --> 00:10:18.010
"This isn't hard." I kept saying,

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:19.397
I was like, "This is not hard.

00:10:19.397 --> 00:10:21.080
"We haven't gotten to anything hard yet."

00:10:21.080 --> 00:10:21.913
He was like--

00:10:21.913 --> 00:10:23.040
I can make it hard if you want.

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:25.140
If you want to make this
difficult, I can do it.

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:26.390
I wasn't there yet.

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:29.087
And he was like, "Well,
it's hot, and this is hard."

00:10:29.959 --> 00:10:31.700
And he kept having to stop

00:10:31.700 --> 00:10:33.560
and then he would stop and
he would push his bike,

00:10:33.560 --> 00:10:35.817
like on a flat surface, and I was like,

00:10:35.817 --> 00:10:39.340
"Shepherd, you're not getting a new bike."

00:10:39.340 --> 00:10:42.167
It's like I was like,
"You're not listening to me.

00:10:42.167 --> 00:10:43.617
"You're not standing up.

00:10:43.617 --> 00:10:46.177
"You're not doing any of the
stuff that I asked you to do.

00:10:46.177 --> 00:10:47.650
"And so I'm not getting you a new bike."

00:10:47.650 --> 00:10:49.130
And then he just had this look of defeat.

00:10:49.130 --> 00:10:50.250
I felt bad.

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:52.890
But I was also like, I was texting Jessie.

00:10:52.890 --> 00:10:54.830
Tough love, you went with tough Love.

00:10:54.830 --> 00:10:55.850
I was texting Jessie

00:10:55.850 --> 00:10:58.170
and I was like, "We got to do something.

00:10:58.170 --> 00:11:00.790
"We got to send him to
bike school or something

00:11:00.790 --> 00:11:01.907
because Dad is failing.

00:11:01.907 --> 00:11:03.545
"I don't know what to do."

00:11:03.545 --> 00:11:04.686
I'm feel like I'm losing control.

00:11:04.686 --> 00:11:05.590
I know some bikes schools,

00:11:05.590 --> 00:11:06.810
if you want me to write them down for you,

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:10.010
And then we get to this long straightaway

00:11:10.010 --> 00:11:11.580
There's a bike school.

00:11:11.580 --> 00:11:12.480
This probably is one.

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:13.930
Shepherd, I'm like,

00:11:13.930 --> 00:11:15.187
There's this long
straightaway, and I'm like,

00:11:15.187 --> 00:11:18.517
