00:13:23.310 --> 00:13:24.650
if you want to abandon your son.

00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:26.887
So I go to him and I say,

00:13:26.887 --> 00:13:30.090
"Shepherd, I don't know
what happened today

00:13:31.397 --> 00:13:34.137
"but we got to get back to the car."

00:13:35.050 --> 00:13:37.600
And so we start pushing the bikes.

00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:38.450
And I'm still thinking about

00:13:38.450 --> 00:13:40.210
like fatherly things to say and

00:13:40.210 --> 00:13:43.240
how do I send a message here?

00:13:43.240 --> 00:13:45.470
How do I give him an
opportunity to want to,

00:13:45.470 --> 00:13:49.940
I'm thinking about preserving
his desire to bicycle.

00:13:49.940 --> 00:13:50.773
You know what I'm saying?

00:13:50.773 --> 00:13:53.290
We're in that state at this point.

00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:55.880
And so I'm like, you know
what, he's going very slow.

00:13:55.880 --> 00:13:57.067
I'm like, "Let me push your bike.

00:13:57.067 --> 00:13:58.427
"I'll push both of our bikes #

00:13:58.427 --> 00:14:00.107
