That's not how it works,
you got to just do it.

00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:55.840
We'll you still got the old bike.

00:20:55.840 --> 00:20:58.660
Yeah, I do, but I have to fix that.

00:20:58.660 --> 00:20:59.880
I mean, it wouldn't be that hard to do,

00:20:59.880 --> 00:21:02.090
but I just, I'm so mad at that bike.

00:21:02.090 --> 00:21:05.763
Are you mad at the bike,
or you mad at someone else?

00:21:07.010 --> 00:21:08.000
It's one of those things that

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:10.530
when you're in the midst of quarantine,

00:21:10.530 --> 00:21:12.670
and I think that everyone,

00:21:12.670 --> 00:21:15.440
the thing that we've been noticing is

00:21:16.410 --> 00:21:18.960
the family has just never been
around each other this much.

00:21:18.960 --> 00:21:20.160
Oh gosh, I know it.

00:21:20.160 --> 00:21:21.570
And you're just like,
usually there would be

00:21:21.570 --> 00:21:23.170
somebody would go somewhere,

00:21:23.170 --> 00:21:27.200
like a kid would go
someplace, school or anything.

00:21:27.200 --> 00:21:28.033
I've just learned that

00:21:28.033 --> 00:21:31.920
going places and interacting
and doing other things,

00:21:31.920 --> 00:21:33.780
really, even if you're an introvert,

00:21:33.780 --> 00:21:35.530
there's got to be a certain level of

00:21:35.530 --> 00:21:39.060
at least getting away from
the people in your home

00:21:39.060 --> 00:21:42.120
that then it's nice to realize

00:21:42.120 --> 00:21:45.350
those more world than just
the people in your own home.

00:21:45.350 --> 00:21:48.640
I mean, the thing that
resonates with me is

00:21:48.640 --> 00:21:52.700
the first week of quarantine
I'm getting water and ice

00:21:52.700 --> 00:21:56.060
out of the friggin fridge and
there's no ice in the whole,

00:21:56.060 --> 00:21:57.310
my ice makers broken.

00:21:57.310 --> 00:21:59.123
I haven't had ice the whole time.

00:21:59.123 --> 00:22:00.280
This whole time?

00:22:00.280 --> 00:22:01.430
Because I didn't want to call someone

00:22:01.430 --> 00:22:02.630
to come in the house and fix it's

00:22:02.630 --> 00:22:04.020
It's like the 1700s with your house.

00:22:04.020 --> 00:22:07.910
We had, we're pouring ice
into the little things

00:22:07.910 --> 00:22:10.090
and then not refilling it,
but leaving it in there

00:22:10.090 --> 00:22:11.287
so that when someone goes for ice

00:22:11.287 --> 00:22:15.220
and it's just an empty tray
with no water or ice in it,

00:22:15.220 --> 00:22:16.420
everybody gets upset.

00:22:16.420 --> 00:22:19.910
And then all this winds coming through.

00:22:19.910 --> 00:22:22.560
And I look outside yesterday and the tree

00:22:22.560 --> 00:22:25.780
in front of my house, the
little tree that staked down.

00:22:25.780 --> 00:22:28.120
It's like a seven foot tall
tree, but still pretty thin.

00:22:28.120 --> 00:22:30.180
It's blown over because

00:22:30.180 --> 00:22:33.310
the stake that was holding it up broke.

00:22:33.310 --> 00:22:36.700
And here I am, I can't,

00:22:36.700 --> 00:22:38.267
I'm trying to like re-stake the tree,

00:22:38.267 --> 00:22:39.790
and I can't even do it.

00:22:39.790 --> 00:22:41.820
Like we're not men anymore, man.

00:22:41.820 --> 00:22:44.390
We can't do stuff that we thought that

00:22:44.390 --> 00:22:46.390
you're supposed to be,
oh, the tree fell over

00:22:46.390 --> 00:22:48.520
or the bikes in a box.

00:22:48.520 --> 00:22:50.190
That's fine.

00:22:50.190 --> 00:22:53.392
My son is a disappointment,
I can fix this.

00:22:53.392 --> 00:22:55.675
I did do plumbing, I did
plumbing this past weekend.

00:22:55.675 --> 00:22:57.470
You did plumbing?

00:22:57.470 --> 00:23:00.623
The garbage disposal had
come loose and was leaking.

00:23:01.670 --> 00:23:03.060
You tightened something.

00:23:03.060 --> 00:23:05.020
Well no, it fell off completely.

00:23:05.020 --> 00:23:05.853
Oh wow.

00:23:05.853 --> 00:23:09.100
And I did, and I watched
a YouTube video for that

00:23:09.100 --> 00:23:12.910
and I got to a place where
I was about to tell Jessie

00:23:12.910 --> 00:23:14.223
we have to call a plumber.

00:23:16.150 --> 00:23:18.450
But I did it, I did it and
I was so proud of myself.

00:23:18.450 --> 00:23:20.423
It feels good, but it's just hard.

00:23:20.423 --> 00:23:23.020
It's hard to actually get stuff done

00:23:23.020 --> 00:23:24.433
and not screw it up.

00:23:25.620 --> 00:23:28.260
I mean, kids included.

00:23:28.260 --> 00:23:31.470
Everybody's fuse is a little bit shorter.

00:23:31.470 --> 00:23:35.140
And it's gonna take some kind of,

00:23:35.140 --> 00:23:37.010
like I know we're both
thinking about doing

00:23:37.010 --> 00:23:41.350
some kind of vacation, like
local, somewhere in California

00:23:41.350 --> 00:23:45.480
maybe taking a vacation
at some point, but boy.

00:23:45.480 --> 00:23:47.250
It might be five separate vacations.

00:23:47.250 --> 00:23:48.410
I think we need that.

00:23:48.410 --> 00:23:50.410
I'm gonna call it a firework vacation

00:23:50.410 --> 00:23:52.060
where it's like, "Okay, go."

00:23:52.060 --> 00:23:54.473
And then everybody just goes
in a different direction.

00:23:55.560 --> 00:23:56.840
call that the firework.

00:23:56.840 --> 00:23:58.430
Yeah, how do you take a vacation and then

00:23:58.430 --> 00:24:00.192
just leave your kid somewhere,

00:24:00.192 --> 00:24:01.433
We got to start figuring that out.

00:24:01.433 --> 00:24:04.100
I think all of this, again,

00:24:04.100 --> 00:24:06.900
really brings me back to appreciating

00:24:06.900 --> 00:24:09.150
the spaces that we haven't
been able to enjoy,

00:24:09.150 --> 00:24:13.350
like being back here and our offices

00:24:13.350 --> 00:24:16.260
and stuff like that, which is
what we want to talk about.

00:24:16.260 --> 00:24:17.470
So we'll get to it.

00:24:17.470 --> 00:24:21.720
But first, we're going to
give you an opportunity

00:24:21.720 --> 00:24:24.630
to just spy the shirt
that Link is wearing.

00:24:24.630 --> 00:24:27.440
You might remember that
was a there was a time,

00:24:27.440 --> 00:24:29.660
there was a time on
this particular podcast

00:24:29.660 --> 00:24:31.930
where we would answer your questions

00:24:31.930 --> 00:24:34.220
and then we would leave you
with a little catchphrase.

00:24:34.220 --> 00:24:35.300
Good luck with that.

